/bin/zsh -lc "/Users/omar/.codex/skills/openpencil/scripts/openpencil-cli.sh board build --fresh-context \\
  --runtime-instance-id 'local-authority:local-authority-f06b17af-2b12-4b51-8e75-49506e084910' \\
  --workspace-id 'workspace-44c2b737-ada8-4e45-b8d9-1d30aadf4fdc' \\
  --document-id 'document-1b633407-6552-4f35-a64b-7ac3899a306d' \\
  --content-document-id 'document-1b633407-6552-4f35-a64b-7ac3899a306d' \\
  --page-id '0:2569' \\
  --request-id 'ocean-cleanup-portfolio-2m-20260730-v1' \\
  --intent 'Create an editable board brief comparing three ocean-cleanup programs and recommending a guarded two-million-dollar portfolio.' \\
  --plan-file - --json <<'JSON'
{
  \"contract\": \"board-build-plan/v1\",
  \"artifacts\": [
    {
      \"alias\": \"title\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_text\",
        \"text\": \"OCEAN CLEANUP • "'$2M PORTFOLIO DECISION'"\\nBoard brief | 12-month deployment | Approve a diversified, milestone-gated mix\",
        \"placement\": {\"target\": {\"kind\": \"auto\"}}
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"river\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"1 — River interception | "'$900k",
        "body": "THE OCEAN CLEANUP — INTERCEPTOR PROGRAM'"\\n\\nIMPACT\\nStops leakage before it reaches the ocean. The program reported 11.6M kg of river catch in 2024.\\n\\n12-MONTH FUNDING CASE\\n• 45% of portfolio\\n• Target: ≥900k lb verified catch\\n• Gate: ≤"'$1.00 per verified lb'"\\n• Operating target: ≥75% uptime\\n\\nEXECUTION RISK — HIGH\\nPermits, floods, machinery, local operator capacity, and waste off-take can delay or strand assets.\\n\\nFUND ONLY IF\\nA top-leakage site has a signed operator, disposal/off-take plan, permits path, and composition audit.\\n\\nEvidence anchor: The Ocean Cleanup 2024 Annual Report and #TeamSeas verified "'$1-per-pound model."
      }
    },
    {
      "alias": "ghost",
      "recipe": {
        "kind": "native_card",
        "title": "2 — Ghost gear | $700k",
        "body": "GLOBAL GHOST GEAR INITIATIVE — PREVENT + REMOVE'"\\n\\nIMPACT\\nTargets fishing gear that keeps trapping wildlife after loss; pairs retrieval with prevention and fisher adoption. NOAA-backed Ocean Conservancy work targets 600k lb and at least 80 removal events nationally.\\n\\n12-MONTH FUNDING CASE\\n• 35% of portfolio\\n• 5–7 local awards of roughly "'$75k–$125k'"\\n• Target: ≥100k lb verified removal\\n• Gate: ≤"'$7.00 per verified lb for removal'"\\n• Plus: 2 fisheries adopt marking, return, or loss-prevention practice\\n\\nEXECUTION RISK — MEDIUM-HIGH\\nVessel/diver safety, uncertain locations, weather windows, permits, and prevention attribution.\\n\\nFUND ONLY IF\\nLocal fishers co-design the work and every pound has retrieval, disposal/recycling, and safety evidence.\\n\\nEvidence anchor: NOAA Marine Debris Program project page; GGGI best-practice and grant model.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"coastal\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"3 — Coastal cleanup + data | "'$400k",
        "body": "OCEAN CONSERVANCY — INTERNATIONAL COASTAL CLEANUP'"\\n\\nIMPACT\\nFast, distributed removal plus item-level evidence for source reduction. In 2024, 486k volunteers collected 7.4M lb globally.\\n\\n12-MONTH FUNDING CASE\\n• 20% of portfolio\\n• Target: ≥400k lb verified removal\\n• Gate: ≤"'$1.00 per verified lb'"\\n• Data: ≥95% geotagged and itemized across 15 priority sites\\n• Convert findings into 3 policy or waste-system referrals\\n\\nEXECUTION RISK — LOW-MEDIUM\\nMature field model, but volunteer variability, repeat accumulation, disposal quality, and weak counterfactuals reduce leverage.\\n\\nFUND ONLY IF\\nSites are leakage hot spots, disposal is secured, and Clean Swell-compatible reporting is mandatory.\\n\\nEvidence anchor: Ocean Conservancy 2024 ICC toplines, released 2025.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"mix\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"RECOMMENDATION — approve 45 / 35 / 20\",
        \"body\": \""'$900k RIVERS  |  $700k GHOST GEAR  |  $400k COASTAL DATA'"\\n\\nWHY THIS MIX\\nMaximize verified near-term mass without letting tonnage crowd out high-harm gear or the local evidence needed to prevent repeat leakage.\\n\\nPORTFOLIO AMBITION\\n≥1.4M lb intercepted/removed in 12 months, plus 2 fishery prevention systems and 15 mapped coastal hot spots.\\n\\nPAYMENT SHAPE\\n60% at award • 20% at mobilization + measurement readiness • 20% after verified milestone. Holdbacks remain inside the "'$2M.'"\\n\\nBOARD DEBATE\\nMove "'$200k from Rivers to Ghost Gear only if biodiversity harm reduction is valued above near-term mass. Keep all three lanes funded."
      }
    },
    {
      "alias": "rules",
      "recipe": {
        "kind": "native_card",
        "title": "DECISION RULES — approve, stop, reallocate",
        "body": "1. ELIGIBILITY GATE'"\\nNo award without baseline, permits path, safety plan, local operator, waste destination, and measurement protocol.\\n\\n2. VALUE GATE\\nPay for verified outcomes—not devices installed, events held, or volunteers recruited. Score ghost-gear prevention separately from removal mass.\\n\\n3. DAY-90 STOP RULE\\nPause the next tranche for a >60-day slip, an unclosed safety/compliance issue, or projected cost per verified lb above 2× the lane gate.\\n\\n4. REALLOCATION RULE\\nAt day 90, move up to "'$200k to the strongest lane. Preserve all three lanes; cap any lane at 55% and any geography at 35%.'"\\n\\n5. INTEGRITY RULE\\nQuarterly public dashboard, no double-counting, weight composition checks, and chain-of-custody through disposal or recycling.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"week1\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"FIRST WEEK — three actions\",
        \"body\": \"1 — DAY 1 | NAME THE DEAL TEAM\\nAppoint one investment lead and one independent technical reviewer. Lock the scorecard and conflict policy.\\n\\n2 — DAYS 2–4 | RUN A 72-HOUR DATA REQUEST\\nAsk the three program operators for named sites, unit economics, 12-month pipeline, permits, safety, measurement, disposal, and local-partner letters. Normalize replies in one table.\\n\\n3 — DAY 7 | AUTHORIZE CONDITIONAL TERM SHEETS\\nBoard approves allocation bands, first tranches, fallback projects, and the day-90 reallocation authority. Stress-test a 20% overrun and 90-day delay before signature.\\n\\nWEEK-ONE OUTPUT\\nThree comparable dossiers, one red-flag log, and a go / conditional / no-go decision for each lane.\"
      }
    }
  ],
  \"connections\": [],
  \"layout\": {
    \"kind\": \"grid\",
    \"anchor\": {\"alias\": \"title\"},
    \"members\": [\"river\", \"ghost\", \"coastal\", \"mix\", \"rules\", \"week1\"],
    \"columns\": 3,
    \"column_gap\": 56,
    \"row_gap\": 56,
    \"align\": \"start\",
    \"placement\": {\"clearance\": 80, \"preferred_directions\": [\"below\"]}
  }
}
JSON"

